                <pb facs="0278" n="182" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg182"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.00/567: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">McMillin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-12-06T09:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">December 6,
                                1921—9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:30
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>47. A revolution through the Army began at midnight ending five this morning
                    overthrowing Herrera government. Generals Orellana, Lima, and Larrave head a
                    provisional government. President Herrera prisoner in his home. All his Cabinet
                    in military prison. About a dozen killed by police resistance. Many natives
                    arrested. City quiet.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">McMillin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
